<!--
	PrimeFaces SAIL conformance for converters: timestamps (kitchensink.ConvertersFixture, an attribute per converter).
	Records a, b and c (and d and e for the duration) are typed into each field, and into an inline grid row with the
	next record's values, then checked with testValue after the save and once reopened from the list. Then each
	column is filtered in the Vue list grid (the list view) and in the PrimeFaces data table (ConvertersDataTables),
	with values written as the cells show them, and the rows each filter leaves are checked. The values catch day and
	month swapped, 12 hour times at PM, noon and midnight, month names, seconds, negatives, separators, $, percentages
	(over 1000% too), rounding, durations rounded to the minute, and the absolute converter of a stored negative.
	Equals compares the stored value exactly, so a value shown rounded is not filtered by what it shows.
	Run by PrimeFacesConvertersSailIT.
-->
